Input: {"question": "Who is the artist of the album \"Giant Steps\"?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d00", "start": 0, "end": 148, "text": "Giant Steps Giant Steps is the fifth studio album by jazz musician John Coltrane as leader, released in 1960 on Atlantic Records, catalogue SD 1311."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d00", "start": 149, "end": 219, "text": "This was his first album as leader for his new label Atlantic Records."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d00", "start": 220, "end": 292, "text": "Many of its tracks have become practice templates for jazz saxophonists."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d00", "start": 293, "end": 424, "text": "In 2004, it was one of fifty recordings chosen that year by the Library of Congress to be added to the National Recording Registry."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d00", "start": 425, "end": 582, "text": "In 1959, Miles Davis's business manager Harold Lovett negotiated a record contract for Coltrane with Atlantic, the terms including a $7,000 annual guarantee."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d00", "start": 583, "end": 608, "text": "Initial sessions for this"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d01", "start": 0, "end": 147, "text": "Miles Davis - Giant Steps ( Atlantic Records ) | Album Review Close Search Type your search terms above and press return to see the search results."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d01", "start": 148, "end": 425, "text": "Best of Jazz Menu About Jazz Around the World Clubs & Venues Reviews 2020s 2010s 2000s 1990s Search March 8, 2023 comment 0 Miles Davis – Giant Steps There is a well-known Latin phrase Omne trium perfectum which put simply, means “ everything that comes in threes is perfect ”."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d01", "start": 426, "end": 531, "text": "Nobody knows where the principle of the perfect set of three originally came from but it is a philosophy."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d02", "start": 0, "end": 104, "text": "Giant Steps (The Boo Radleys album) Giant Steps is the third album by The Boo Radleys, released in 1993."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d02", "start": 105, "end": 311, "text": "The title is inspired by John Coltrane's album of the same name, and the record features an assortment of influences — their previous shoegazing sound backed by pop, reggae, noise pop and orchestral sounds."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d02", "start": 312, "end": 423, "text": "\"NME\" and \"Select\" named it as album of the year, and it was ranked as #1 in Fanning's Fab Fifty for that year."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d02", "start": 424, "end": 484, "text": "It reached the UK Top 20, but did not spawn a Top 40 single."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d02", "start": 485, "end": 550, "text": "Reviewing the album's rerelease in 2008, Sic Magazine wrote, \"For"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d03", "start": 0, "end": 222, "text": "International Publishing Group Paperback : 956 pages ( Writer/broadcaster/jazz historian Shipton offers a musical analysis of âGiant Steps.â ) See the Reading and Research page for this tune for additional references ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0153-00ae5a2824c1:d03", "start": 223, "end": 428, "text": "- Sandra Burlingame Jazz History Notes Woody Herman -- clarinetist , vocalist , saxophonist and bandleader -- kept a vibrant big band together for 51 years , an achievement equaled only by Duke Ellington ."},